{{- /*
product_edit.gohtml is the panel's only WRITE form (ADR 0013).

Two things about it are load-bearing:

  - The method is POST and the target is inside the panel tree. That is what
    puts the request through the panel's origin check, which has no exemption
    for state-changing requests: SameSite=Strict closes most of CSRF and the
    Origin header closes the subdomain case it leaves open.
  - There is no hidden token field. The protection is the cookie's scope plus
    the origin check, not a token the page has to generate, store and print —
    the decision and its rejected alternative are in ADR 0011.

The status is a <select> over the values the module accepts. A free text field
would send the operator's typo to the module and answer with a rejection they
could have been spared.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<p><a href="{{ .CancelPath }}">← Back to the product</a></p>

<h1>Edit product</h1>
{{ if .Error }}<p role="alert">{{ .Error }}</p>{{ end }}

<form method="post" action="{{ .ActionPath }}">
  <label>Title
    <input type="text" name="title" value="{{ .Product.Title }}" required>
  </label>
  <label>Handle
    <input type="text" name="handle" value="{{ .Product.Handle }}" required>
  </label>
  <label>Status
    <select name="status">
      {{ $current := .Product.Status }}
      {{ range .Statuses }}
        <option value="{{ . }}"{{ if eq . $current }} selected{{ end }}>{{ . }}</option>
      {{ end }}
    </select>
  </label>
  <button type="submit">Save</button>
  <a href="{{ .CancelPath }}">Cancel</a>
</form>
{{ end }}
